{
  "recommendation": "Open a Gold Account (savings) and get the Bronze Rewards Card (personal, no annual fee).",
  "why": "The KB shows the Gold Account has the highest documented base APY (5.50%). The Bronze Rewards Card is explicitly listed in the KB as a no-annual-fee personal card and provides a +0.15% APY bonus on the Gold Account. That combination gives a guaranteed, fee-free boost.",
  "net_return_estimate": {
    "principal": 20000,
    "effective_apy_percent": 5.65,
    "interest_earned_over_1_year_usd": 1130
  },
  "alternative_note": "The KB also shows the EcoCard gives a larger documented APY bonus on the Gold Account (+0.60%), which would raise the effective APY to 6.10% (≈ $1,220 interest on $20,000). However, the KB does NOT include EcoCard’s annual fee. If EcoCard’s annual fee is less than ≈ $90, EcoCard+Gold would beat Bronze+Gold net of fees. Because the KB doesn't list card annual fees, I can't definitively pick a premium card without that fee data.",
  "premium_cards_note": "Top-tier cards (e.g., Diamond Elite, Platinum) sometimes give sizable APY bonuses but frequently have annual fees. The KB documents their bonuses but does not provide a complete set of annual-fee figures, so a premium card could be better or worse depending on its fee and your card-spend rewards — I can't assume fees or spending returns.",
  "next_steps_options": {
    "A": "I can search the KB again for any card-fee info (I already searched and did not find fee amounts).",
    "B": "If you want an exact net-dollar-maximizing pick that accounts for card annual fees and your expected spend, I can transfer you to a human agent who can access live pricing and promotions. (I’ll transfer only if you want.)",
    "C": "If you want me to proceed to open the Gold Account + Bronze Rewards Card for you, I can — but I’ll need to verify your identity first (KB requires verification before opening accounts)."
  },
  "ask": "Which next step would you like? (A, B, or C)"
}

{
  "recommendation": "Gold Account (savings) + EcoCard (credit card)",
  "short_summary": "This combo maximizes the savings APY (Gold base 5.50% + EcoCard bonus +0.60% = 6.10% APY) and also gives card rewards on your spending. After a reasonable assumed EcoCard annual fee and your expected card spend, it produces the highest projected net return on $20,000 held 1 year.",
  "basis_from_KB": {
    "gold_base_apy": "5.50% (Gold Account base APY documented in KB)",
    "eco_card_savings_bonus": "+0.60% on Gold Account (EcoCard documented in KB)",
    "eco_card_rewards": "EcoCard earns sustainability points: 5 pts/$ on green purchases, 1 pt/$ on other purchases; 1 point = $0.01 when redeemed (KB)"
  },
  "assumptions_i_make_and_why": {
    "reason_for_assuming_fees": "KB does not list EcoCard annual fee. You asked me to pick a best single combo including annual fee, so I must assume a reasonable fee and show sensitivity.",
    "eco_card_annual_fee_assumed": 95,
    "why_assumed_95": "A $95 annual fee is a common mid-tier annual fee for premium-but-not-invitation-only cards. It’s conservative enough to represent a paid card without assuming an extremely high premium-fee card (which would require KB confirmation).",
    "cashback_assumption_for_spend": "Assume EcoCard gives 1% cashback on the portion of your groceries/gas that are not 'green' purchases (per KB: 1 point/$ = $0.01). For this calculation I assume your spending is non-green by default; if you have many green-certified purchases a portion could earn 5% equivalent (per KB) which increases net return accordingly."
  },
  "inputs_used": {
    "principal": 20000,
    "time_horizon": "1 year",
    "spend_scenarios_annual": {
      "low": 12000,
      "mid": 18000,
      "high": 24000
    }
  },
  "detailed_math_and_results": {
    "interest_components": {
      "gold_base_interest": 1100,
      "eco_card_savings_bonus_interest": 120,
      "total_interest_before_cashback_fees": 1220
    },
    "cashback_values": {
      "low_spend_12k_at_1%": 120,
      "mid_spend_18k_at_1%": 180,
      "high_spend_24k_at_1%": 240
    },
    "annual_fee_used": 95,
    "net_return_estimates (interest + cashback - assumed fee)": {
      "low_spend_12k": 1220 + 120 - 95,
      "low_spend_12k_value": 1245,
      "mid_spend_18k": 1220 + 180 - 95,
      "mid_spend_18k_value": 1305,
      "high_spend_24k": 1220 + 240 - 95,
      "high_spend_24k_value": 1365
    },
    "comparison_point (no-fee alternative per KB)": {
      "bronze_rewards_card_plus_gold_account": {
        "bronze_bonus_on_gold": "+0.15% (KB)",
        "effective_apy_percent": 5.65,
        "interest_on_20k": 1130,
        "annual_fee": 0,
        "net_return_if_no_card_cashback_is_counted": 1130
      }
    }
  },
  "break_even_analysis_vs_bronze+gold": {
    "extra_interest_from_eco_vs_bronze": 90,
    "break_even_fee_formula": "break_even_fee = extra_interest (90) + expected_cashback",
    "break_even_examples": {
      "if_spend_12k (cashback 120)": 90 + 120,
      "break_even_fee_12k_value": 210,
      "if_spend_18k (cashback 180)": 90 + 180,
      "break_even_fee_18k_value": 270,
      "if_spend_24k (cashback 240)": 90 + 240,
      "break_even_fee_24k_value": 330
    },
    "interpretation": "If EcoCard’s true annual fee is below the break-even number for your expected spend, EcoCard+Gold yields a higher net return than the safe Bronze+Gold no-fee route. With my assumed $95 fee, EcoCard wins comfortably for all spend levels you gave."
  },
  "caveats_and_notes": [
    "KB does NOT provide EcoCard annual-fee data. I assumed $95 and showed sensitivity. If the actual EcoCard fee is higher than the break-even for your spend level (210/270/330 for the 12k/18k/24k scenarios above), the recommendation may change.",
    "If a large share of your card spend is 'green' (eligible at 5% per KB), your cashback will be substantially higher and further favor EcoCard.",
    "I focused on maximizing net dollars (interest + card cash back − card fee). I did not recommend opening a new checking account because you said you won't; some checking+ savings pairings could provide linked boosts but you said you won't open another checking account.",
    "If you want a strictly no-fee guarantee, Bronze Rewards Card + Gold Account is the safe alternative (KB shows Bronze is no-annual-fee and gives +0.15% on Gold)."
  ],
  "final_recommendation_and_actionable": {
    "pick": "Gold Account + EcoCard",
    "why_one_sentence": "Highest documented Gold base APY + largest documented card APY bonus (EcoCard +0.60%) plus EcoCard reward points on spending — with a reasonable assumed annual fee ($95) this yields the highest net dollars for your $20,000 over one year in the spend range you gave.",
    "if_you_agree_next_steps": "I can: (A) try another KB search for live EcoCard annual-fee details (KB previously had no fee info), or (B) if you want to open these I must verify your identity per KB procedures before opening accounts. Which would you like?"
  }
}

{
  "recommendation": "EcoCard (credit card) + Silver Account (savings)",
  "one_line_rationale": "For a $20,000 balance left untouched for one year, the KB shows Silver base APY = 4.00% (tier applies at ≥ $10,000) and EcoCard provides a documented +2.20% APY bonus on Silver — giving an effective APY of 6.20%, which yields the highest one-year dollar return versus the other savings options in the KB.",
  "calculation": {
    "silver_base_apy_percent": 4.00,
    "ecocard_bonus_on_silver_percent": 2.20,
    "effective_apy_percent": 6.20,
    "principal_usd": 20000,
    "interest_earned_one_year_usd": 1240,
    "comparison_other_cases": {
      "gold + ecocard": {
        "gold_base_apy_percent": 5.50,
        "ecocard_bonus_on_gold_percent": 0.60,
        "effective_apy_percent": 6.10,
        "interest_earned_one_year_usd": 1220
      },
      "bronze(no-fee card) + gold": {
        "effective_apy_percent": 5.65,
        "interest_earned_one_year_usd": 1130
      }
    },
    "net_difference_vs_gold_ecocard_usd": 20
  },
  "key_kb_sources_used": [
    {
      "doc": "Silver Account - interest & bonuses",
      "note": "Shows Silver tiers (2.5% / 4.0%) and lists EcoCard credit-card APY bonus = +2.2% on Silver."
    },
    {
      "doc": "Silver tier thresholds / calculation",
      "note": "Explains Silver's tier threshold (daily balance compared to $10,000) — your $20,000 qualifies for the 4.0% base."
    },
    {
      "doc": "Gold Account - base APY and EcoCard bonus",
      "note": "Shows Gold base APY = 5.50% and EcoCard bonus on Gold = +0.60% (used for comparison)."
    }
  ],
  "important_caveats": [
    "The KB does NOT list EcoCard annual fee in the searchable docs I retrieved. Because you're comparing EcoCard+Silver vs EcoCard+Gold the same card/fee would apply to both combos and therefore cancels out when choosing between those two — the savings APY difference decides the winner.",
    "If you instead compare EcoCard+Silver to a no-annual-fee-card alternative (e.g., Bronze+Gold), the EcoCard annual fee matters for net return. If you want, I can try to locate current card-fee info or escalate to a human to fetch live pricing.",
    "The Silver Account APY is tiered by daily balance; with $20,000 you meet the Silver higher tier (4.0%) as documented.",
    "If a material share of your card spending is eligible for EcoCard's higher 'green' earn rate (per KB the EcoCard awards higher points on green-certified purchases), your card rewards increase but that does not change the Silver-vs-Gold savings-APY winner because the same card would be used."
  ],
  "next_steps_if_you_want_to_proceed": {
    "open_accounts": "I can open the Silver Account and request an EcoCard for you. Per KB procedure I must verify your identity before opening accounts.",
    "identity_verification_requirements": "I will need you to confirm any 2 of the following: date of birth, email, phone number, or address (this is required by our agent procedures before accessing/creating account records). After verification I will follow the account-opening flow.",
    "alternative": "If you'd like, I can first try to find the EcoCard's live annual fee in our KB or escalate to a human agent to confirm current card fees and promotions before opening anything."
  },
  "ask": "Do you want me to proceed with EcoCard + Silver Account now? If yes, do you want me to (A) verify your identity and open the accounts, or (B) look up the EcoCard annual fee first (KB didn't show it)? Please reply A or B." 
}
